
**Required output format (structural audit — MANDATORY):**

End with exactly one fenced JSON object and emit no textual decision line.
Implementation authority is represented only by the live GitHub
implementation-state label after the PR exists; this pre-PR compatibility
review remains informational.

```json
{"grade": "A", "summary": "...", "comments": [
  {"path": "...", "line": 1, "side": "RIGHT", "severity": "major", "body": "..."}
]}
```

`grade` is one of `A`, `B`, `C`, `D`, `E`, or `F`; `summary` is a concise
informational summary; and `comments` is an array of concrete findings. Each
comment must provide a repository-relative `path`, positive changed-line
`line`, `"RIGHT"` side, one of `critical`, `major`, `minor`, or `nitpick`
severity, and actionable `body`. Emit an empty `comments` array only when no
findings remain. Do not emit `Verdict:` or any other approval/rejection token.
